# terraform-provider-gpupaas — provider resource workflow

This provider is a **thin Terraform-Plugin-Framework adapter** over the
`gpupaas-go` SDK. It never talks HTTP directly and never invents fields the SDK
does not expose.

## SDK-first ordering

The SDK is the source of truth. If the backend API changed, update
`../gpupaas-go` **first** (see its `add-resource-from-swagger` SKILL), then
surface the change here. Do not add a Terraform resource for an API the SDK does
not model yet.

## Always follow these docs

- **Workflow (exact steps):** `specs/add-resource-from-sdk/SKILL.md`
- **Design patterns / steering:** `specs/terraform-provider/steering/`
  (`project-overview.md`, `architecture-patterns.md`, `coding-standards.md`)
- **Authoritative resource catalog:** `../gpupaas-go/README.md` (Appendix) and
  `../gpupaas-go/clientset/typed/v1alpha1/interfaces.go` (action verbs). When in
  doubt, the Go types win over the README.

## Pipeline (per kind)

```
internal/provider/resources/<kind>_resource.go        CRUD + Import
internal/provider/resources/<kind>_data_source.go      read-by-name lookup
internal/provider/resources/<kind>_status_data_source.go  only if SDK has live GetStatus
internal/provider/provider.go                          register resource + data sources
internal/client/fake.go                                must satisfy the FULL typed interface
examples/resources/gpupaas_<kind>/                     resource.tf (+ import.sh)
examples/data-sources/...                              data-source.tf
docs/                                                  via `tfplugindocs generate`
```

## Patterns (hard requirements)

- **Naming:** `gpupaas_<snake_case>` from the SDK Kind. Status data sources use
  the `_status` suffix.
- **Envelope schema:** `metadata` / `spec` / `status`. Set `api_version` and
  `kind` internally as `Computed`, never user-required.
- **Status is `Computed: true`**, field-for-field mirror of `apiv1.<Kind>Status`;
  never write it back to the SDK.
- **Imperative verbs → a single `desired_action`** string attribute with an
  `OneOf` validator sourced from the typed interface, plus an optional
  `action_inputs` nested block. The `Update` method diffs old vs. new
  `desired_action` and dispatches the matching SDK call. Never map
  `desired_action` to an SDK spec field; never auto-trigger on refresh.
- **No dedicated SDK Update?** Route spec-only updates through the idempotent
  `Create` (the dev-resource pattern).
- **Import IDs** encode scope: `<name>` / `<project>/<name>` /
  `<project>/<workspace>/<name>`. Use the parsers in `common.go`.
- **Keep the fake exhaustive** — every interface method must exist in
  `internal/client/fake.go` or the build/tests break.
- **Thin adapter** — no HTTP, retry, or auth logic; call the typed clientset.

## Backward compatibility (ask before breaking)

- Never silently remove/rename a Terraform attribute, resource, or data source;
  default to keeping it marked `DeprecationMessage:`.
- Never change an existing import-ID format or a resource's scope without
  explicit approval.

## Dependency wiring

- Local dev: `go.mod` keeps `replace github.com/gpupaas-ai/gpupaas-go => ../gpupaas-go`.
- Before release: `go get github.com/gpupaas-ai/gpupaas-go@vX.Y.Z && go mod tidy`
  and drop the local replace. Don't ship the replace.

## Verify gate (all must pass before reporting done)

```bash
go fmt ./...
go vet ./...
go test ./...      # in-memory fake clientset; no API needed
go build ./...
tfplugindocs generate && git diff docs/   # only intended new files
```

See `DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md` for the full cross-repo workflow and release steps.
